{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509554-how-would-you-calculate-strength-for-telekinesis","id":1509554,"title":"How would you calculate strength for Telekinesis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-24T21:38:37-07:00","id":1509554,"title":"How would you calculate strength for Telekinesis","content":"So, as the title suggests, how would you calculate the &quot;strength&quot; of a Telekinesis pull if a mage uses it to pull another creature against its will?<br /> Say the creature is fighting against it (as they naturally should), so what would the creature resisting roll be in your opinion? Rego Motus's text in Vampire states that if you want to force somebody with it, it's a contested Willpower roll to see if you can control the creature, I don't remember having read anything similar in Mage.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine says the test should be the Strength against the successes in the Mage's test, but I argued that it would almost always give the Mage a huge disadvantage as if you roll 3-5 dices for Arete against the Strength of the creature, that if, for example, is a werewolf or worse a vampire, would make it VERY hard to control. Let's imagine a Theo Bell with Strength 5 (that is, if he doesn't use blood to increase it) and Potence 4 and giving that the Potence could be considered automatic (depending on the ST), it would make it nearly impossible to move him with Telekinesis. I've never found a satisfactory system for such a situation. How would you treat this situation in your games? Have you found a good system for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T21:57:54-07:00","id":1509556,"title":"","content":"There is a line of thaumaturgy that does this more or less that and rule are, each turn both the mage and the trapped target make a test of willpower against willpower, whoever succeeds most wins, I don't know if the difficulty is the opponent's default or willpower of oponent, I think it would be fair for the difficulty for the target to be discipline level or sphere +3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T22:12:08-07:00","id":1509557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509554-how-would-you-calculate-strength-for-telekinesis?p=1509556#post1509556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a line of thaumaturgy that does this more or less that and rule are, each turn both the mage and the trapped target make a test of willpower against willpower, whoever succeeds most wins, I don't know if the difficulty is the opponent's default or willpower of oponent, I think it would be fair for the difficulty for the target to be discipline level or sphere +3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Thaumaturgy Path is <i>Rego Motus</i>, as I said in the post. It's called &quot;Movement of the Mind&quot; in the modern setting. To be fair, I don't think this system is very fair as well, because the chances are basically equal between both sides, Regardless of the power of the one using Telekinesis. It's the system I've been using, but I don't like it at all. It's really hard to find a satisfying one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-25-2023, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T04:16:39-07:00","id":1509572,"title":"","content":"Look, I don't have much practice with this path myself, because I never got to play with anyone who used it, but I can try to make a logical attempt. Have you tried a roll like the victim must escape using Stamina + Survival on a roll difficulty equal to path level +3? The victim need unleast 3 sucesses to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T05:05:39-07:00","id":1509575,"title":"","content":"I think it greatly depends on if the defender sees the attack coming and what capacity he has to resist it. <br /> <br /> In normal circumstances I'd handle this as Dodging a Physical Attack (complete with the Perception + Awareness roll to even detect the attack if they don't already know its coming) with the dodge roll representing the defender getting out of the way or bracing in time. I'd only consider getting into contested strength rolls if the defender is already braced against something and the attacker keeps pulling. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T16:37:40-07:00","id":1509642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509554-how-would-you-calculate-strength-for-telekinesis?p=1509572#post1509572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I don't have much practice with this path myself, because I never got to play with anyone who used it, but I can try to make a logical attempt. Have you tried a roll like the victim must escape using Stamina + Survival on a roll difficulty equal to path level +3? The victim need unleast 3 sucesses to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an idea, but I'm still not sure if it isn't better to just leave it as it is using Willpower, but then requiring a number of successes to be free equal to the level of the Path/Sphere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In normal circumstances I'd handle this as Dodging a Physical Attack (complete with the Perception + Awareness roll to even detect the attack if they don't already know its coming) with the dodge roll representing the defender getting out of the way or bracing in time. I'd only consider getting into contested strength rolls if the defender is already braced against something and the attacker keeps pulling.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>But then if the creature resisting the pull is a vampire, it would be almost impossible for the mage to keep him trapped, in this way I would say that even the contested WP roll benefits the Mage more, as at least chances are basically equal, however unfair it is, it's not nearly as bad as giving the vampire auto successes and a potentially MUCH BIGGER dicepool (even more absurd if the ST makes Potence count as automatic, in this case not even mighty Porthos would have a chance to keep a mere Theo Bell under his Telekinetic pull).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T22:58:07-07:00","id":1509690,"title":"","content":"You could always use the damage done by the number of successes on an Arete roll (with the usual +1 from using Forces) as an effective Str rating of the telekinetic grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T05:06:50-07:00","id":1509704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509554-how-would-you-calculate-strength-for-telekinesis?p=1509642#post1509642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an idea, but I'm still not sure if it isn't better to just leave it as it is using Willpower, but then requiring a number of successes to be free equal to the level of the Path/Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But then if the creature resisting the pull is a vampire, it would be almost impossible for the mage to keep him trapped, in this way I would say that even the contested WP roll benefits the Mage more, as at least chances are basically equal, however unfair it is, it's not nearly as bad as giving the vampire auto successes and a potentially MUCH BIGGER dicepool (even more absurd if the ST makes Potence count as automatic, in this case not even mighty Porthos would have a chance to keep a mere Theo Bell under his Telekinetic pull).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see a problem with supernatural strength providing a counter to telekinesis in the context of bracing. Also remember to factor in the strength of whatever the vampire is bracing against. A vampire's high successes don't do him much good when the railing he's braced against gives way. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is one other system you could use for quick adjudication. I hate referencing How Do You Do That because it is a mess, but there's a chart in there for the lifting values of various levels of Forces. It goes something like this:<br /> <br /> Forces 1: Nothing.<br /> Forces 2: Around 300 pounds.<br /> Forces 3: Around 2 tons<br /> Forces 4: Small buildings<br /> Forces 5: Most things smaller than a mountain<br /> <br /> What you could do is use that chart to determine how many successes someone resisting with raw strength must muster to be able to resist a telekinetic pull. So if the Mage uses Forces 2, the Vampire would need to muster 4 successes. If the Mage uses Forces 3, the vampire would need 12-13. The feats of strength chart doesn't go high enough to cover Forces 4 and 5.<br /> <br /> Is that the kind of scaling you are looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T06:32:03-07:00","id":1509711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509554-how-would-you-calculate-strength-for-telekinesis?p=1509704#post1509704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really see a problem with supernatural strength providing a counter to telekinesis in the context of bracing. Also remember to factor in the strength of whatever the vampire is bracing against. A vampire's high successes don't do him much good when the railing he's braced against gives way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There is one other system you could use for quick adjudication. I hate referencing How Do You Do That because it is a mess, but there's a chart in there for the lifting values of various levels of Forces. It goes something like this:<br /> <br /> Forces 1: Nothing.<br /> Forces 2: Around 300 pounds.<br /> Forces 3: Around 2 tons<br /> Forces 4: Small buildings<br /> Forces 5: Most things smaller than a mountain<br /> <br /> What you could do is use that chart to determine how many successes someone resisting with raw strength must muster to be able to resist a telekinetic pull. So if the Mage uses Forces 2, the Vampire would need to muster 4 successes. If the Mage uses Forces 3, the vampire would need 12-13. The feats of strength chart doesn't go high enough to cover Forces 4 and 5.<br /> <br /> Is that the kind of scaling you are looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a neat idea, I haven't thought about it before. I like it especially because it makes the level of proficiency with the Sphere really count, even if it might sound unfair for a vampire player if the Mage has Forces 4 and then the player would feel a bit underwhelmed if I told him that there's nothing he can do, but in my honest opinion it's fair, perhaps telling the player he needs 20 successes to fight against Forces 4 would make him feel a bit better as at least there's some way for him to visualize it. As the feats of strenght could as well go up a little beyond the 15 strength as there are plenty of vampires out there who could have this amount of successes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could always use the damage done by the number of successes on an Arete roll (with the usual +1 from using Forces) as an effective Str rating of the telekinetic grapple. </div> </div> </div>This is also a great idea, much better than using WP in my opinion, to be fair that was the first one I thought about using, but then I wanted to hear other people's opinion on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T01:02:07-07:00","id":1510868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509554-how-would-you-calculate-strength-for-telekinesis#post1509554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as the title suggests, how would you calculate the &quot;strength&quot; of a Telekinesis pull if a mage uses it to pull another creature against its will?<br /> Say the creature is fighting against it (as they naturally should), so what would the creature resisting roll be in your opinion? Rego Motus's text in Vampire states that if you want to force somebody with it, it's a contested Willpower roll to see if you can control the creature, I don't remember having read anything similar in Mage.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine says the test should be the Strength against the successes in the Mage's test, but I argued that it would almost always give the Mage a huge disadvantage as if you roll 3-5 dices for Arete against the Strength of the creature, that if, for example, is a werewolf or worse a vampire, would make it VERY hard to control. Let's imagine a Theo Bell with Strength 5 (that is, if he doesn't use blood to increase it) and Potence 4 and giving that the Potence could be considered automatic (depending on the ST), it would make it nearly impossible to move him with Telekinesis. I've never found a satisfactory system for such a situation. How would you treat this situation in your games? Have you found a good system for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>How about giving the telekinesis 2 strength per success plus 1 per success on the targeting roll(if there is one) <br /> In regards to rego motus, I would argue that this would go against the spirit of mage. After all, willpower and kinetic force have no relationship (though the hermetic praxis may)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T13:41:36-07:00","id":1510910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In regards to rego motus, I would argue that this would go against the spirit of mage. After all, willpower and kinetic force have no relationship (though the hermetic praxis may) </div> </div> </div>Yes that's one of the reasons why I'm not satisfied with using WP to resist, beyond the fact that it utterly ignores the Mage/Blood Mage proficiency when it comes to resisting it. I believe using the damage table for the &quot;Strength&quot; of the telekinesis is until now the one that makes more sense to me, but your idea is similar, so it also works. I haven't come across such a situation in the game for quite a while, but it's always a possibility and I want to have a better system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}